.TH "MINIOS\-CMD" "1" "September 2026" "MiniOS Command\-Line Builder" ""
.SH NAME
minios\-cmd \- configure and build a MiniOS image
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]minios\-cmd\f[R] [\f[I]OPTIONS\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]minios\-cmd\f[R] is a command\-line frontend for
\f[B]minios\-live\f[R](1).
It copies a configuration template or an existing configuration into a
work directory, applies frontend values, and runs a complete build.
.PP
The default configuration currently lists Debian \f[B]buster\f[R],
\f[B]bullseye\f[R], \f[B]bookworm\f[R], and \f[B]trixie\f[R]; Ubuntu
\f[B]bionic\f[R], \f[B]focal\f[R], \f[B]jammy\f[R], \f[B]noble\f[R], and
\f[B]resolute\f[R]; and Devuan \f[B]beowulf\f[R], \f[B]chimaera\f[R],
\f[B]daedalus\f[R], and \f[B]excalibur\f[R].
It lists \f[B]amd64\f[R], \f[B]i386\f[R], and \f[B]i386\-pae\f[R]
architectures; \f[B]core\f[R], \f[B]flux\f[R], \f[B]xfce\f[R], and
\f[B]lxqt\f[R] environments; \f[B]minimum\f[R], \f[B]standard\f[R],
\f[B]toolbox\f[R], and \f[B]ultra\f[R] variants; and \f[B]xz\f[R],
\f[B]lzo\f[R], \f[B]gz\f[R], \f[B]lz4\f[R], and \f[B]zstd\f[R]
compression.
.PP
Not every combination is necessarily available.
The current configuration, environment links, and repositories determine
what can be built.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
All non\-help operations, including \f[B]\-\-config\-only\f[R],
currently require root.
Source\-tree builds require a Debian or Ubuntu host, the packages in
\f[B]linux\-live/prerequisites.list\f[R], and repository access.
The default template enables apt\-cacher\-ng at
\f[B]127.0.0.1:3142\f[R]; run it or set \f[B]USE_APT_CACHER=false\f[R]
in the generated configuration.
.SH OPTIONS
Without \f[B]\-\-config\-file\f[R], the distribution, architecture,
desktop environment, and package variant options are required.
.SS Configuration Options
.TP
\f[B]\-\-config\-file\f[R] \f[I]FILE\f[R]
In normal mode, copy \f[I]FILE\f[R] into the work directory as the base
configuration, then write parsed frontend values and non\-empty frontend
defaults into that copy.
With \f[B]\-\-config\-only\f[R], use \f[I]FILE\f[R] as the output path
and overwrite it.
To use a configuration without frontend merging, run
\f[B]minios\-live\f[R] directly with \f[B]BUILD_CONF\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\-\-config\-only\f[R]
Generate a configuration file and do not build.
Without \f[B]\-\-config\-file\f[R], the four required system options are
required.
Supplying an output path with \f[B]\-\-config\-file\f[R] bypasses that
check, and omitted target fields retain template values.
.TP
\f[B]\-b\f[R], \f[B]\-\-build\-dir\f[R] \f[I]DIR\f[R]
Use \f[I]DIR\f[R] as the build directory.
.SS System Options
.TP
\f[B]\-d\f[R], \f[B]\-\-distribution\f[R] \f[I]NAME\f[R]
Set the target distribution.
Required without \f[B]\-\-config\-file\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\-a\f[R], \f[B]\-\-architecture\f[R] \f[I]NAME\f[R]
Set the target architecture.
Required without \f[B]\-\-config\-file\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\-de\f[R], \f[B]\-\-desktop\-environment\f[R] \f[I]NAME\f[R]
Set the desktop environment.
Required without \f[B]\-\-config\-file\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\-pv\f[R], \f[B]\-\-package\-variant\f[R] \f[I]NAME\f[R]
Set the package variant.
Required without \f[B]\-\-config\-file\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\-c\f[R], \f[B]\-\-compression\-type\f[R] \f[I]NAME\f[R]
Set SquashFS compression.
Default: \f[B]zstd\f[R].
.SS Kernel Options
.TP
\f[B]\-kp\f[R], \f[B]\-\-kernel\-provider\f[R] \f[I]NAME\f[R]
Select \f[B]distribution\f[R] or \f[B]minios\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\-kf\f[R], \f[B]\-\-kernel\-flavour\f[R] \f[I]NAME\f[R]
Set the kernel flavour, such as \f[B]none\f[R], \f[B]rt\f[R], or
\f[B]cloud\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\-mk\f[R], \f[B]\-\-minios\-kernel\f[R]
Select the MiniOS kernel provider.
.TP
\f[B]\-mks\f[R], \f[B]\-\-minios\-kernel\-series\f[R] \f[I]NAME\f[R]
Select \f[B]auto\f[R], \f[B]6.1\f[R], or \f[B]6.12\f[R] and use the
MiniOS provider.
.TP
\f[B]\-kpm\f[R], \f[B]\-\-kernel\-payload\-mode\f[R] \f[I]NAME\f[R]
Select \f[B]runtime\f[R] or \f[B]full\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\-dkms\f[R], \f[B]\-\-kernel\-build\-dkms\f[R]
Build additional DKMS drivers.
.TP
\f[B]\-aufs\f[R], \f[B]\-\-kernel\-aufs\f[R]
Deprecated alias for \f[B]\-\-minios\-kernel\f[R].
.SS Locale And Boot Options
.TP
\f[B]\-l\f[R], \f[B]\-\-locale\f[R] \f[I]NAME\f[R]
Set the system locale.
Default: \f[B]en_US\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\-ml\f[R], \f[B]\-\-multilingual\f[R]
Generate all locales declared by \f[B]minioslib\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\-kl\f[R], \f[B]\-\-keep\-locales\f[R]
Retain all available locales instead of pruning them.
.TP
\f[B]\-tz\f[R], \f[B]\-\-timezone\f[R] \f[I]NAME\f[R]
Set the timezone.
Default: \f[B]Etc/UTC\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\-ib\f[R], \f[B]\-\-initramfs\-builder\f[R] \f[I]NAME\f[R]
Select \f[B]livekit\f[R] or \f[B]dracut\f[R].
Default: \f[B]dracut\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\-mln\f[R], \f[B]\-\-menu\-language\f[R] \f[I]NAME\f[R]
Select \f[B]multilang\f[R] or a supported menu locale.
Default: \f[B]multilang\f[R].
.SS Ubuntu Pro Option
.TP
\f[B]\-\-ubuntu\-pro\-token\f[R] \f[I]TOKEN\f[R]
Attach an Ubuntu Pro subscription during a Bionic, Focal, Jammy, or
Noble build.
Other targets skip attachment with a warning.
The builder detaches the subscription and removes the token from the
final image.
Command\-line tokens may be visible in shell history or process
listings.
.SH DEFAULTS
The frontend defaults are \f[B]COMP_TYPE=zstd\f[R],
\f[B]KERNEL_PROVIDER=distribution\f[R], \f[B]KERNEL_FLAVOUR=none\f[R],
\f[B]MINIOS_KERNEL_SERIES=auto\f[R],
\f[B]KERNEL_PAYLOAD_MODE=runtime\f[R],
\f[B]KERNEL_BUILD_DKMS=false\f[R], \f[B]LOCALE=en_US\f[R],
\f[B]MULTILINGUAL=false\f[R], \f[B]KEEP_LOCALES=false\f[R],
\f[B]LIVE_TIMEZONE=Etc/UTC\f[R], \f[B]INITRAMFS_BUILDER=dracut\f[R], and
\f[B]MENU_LANG=multilang\f[R].
.PP
Trixie\-based \f[B]i386\f[R] and \f[B]i386\-pae\f[R] values select the
MiniOS provider when the distribution and architecture are supplied to
the frontend through options or the environment.
Values present only inside \f[B]\-\-config\-file\f[R] are not loaded
before defaults are calculated.
Frontend defaults may differ from values in the full
\f[B]build.conf\f[R] template.
.SH EXAMPLES
Build a standard Bookworm Xfce image with frontend defaults:
.IP
.EX
sudo minios\-cmd \-d bookworm \-a amd64 \-de xfce \-pv standard
.EE
.PP
Build with a MiniOS kernel, DKMS drivers, and retained locales:
.IP
.EX
sudo minios\-cmd \-d bookworm \-a amd64 \-de xfce \-pv toolbox \-mk \-dkms \-kl
.EE
.PP
Build a multilingual image:
.IP
.EX
sudo minios\-cmd \-d trixie \-a amd64 \-de xfce \-pv standard \-ml
.EE
.PP
Build the Flux minimum variant with livekit:
.IP
.EX
sudo minios\-cmd \-d bookworm \-a amd64 \-de flux \-pv minimum \-ib livekit
.EE
.PP
Generate or overwrite a configuration file:
.IP
.EX
sudo minios\-cmd \-\-config\-only \-\-config\-file ./myconfig.conf \[rs]
  \-d bookworm \-a amd64 \-de xfce \-pv standard
.EE
.PP
Use the file without frontend merging:
.IP
.EX
sudo BUILD_CONF=/absolute/path/myconfig.conf minios\-live \-
.EE
